DELETE /v1/logs/streams/owner/{ownerId}
Removes the log stream for the specified workspace.
Required: ownerId (path) — The ID of the workspace to delete the log stream for

DELETE /v1/logs/streams/resource/{resourceId}
Removes the log stream override for the specified resource. After deletion, the resource will use the workspace's default log stream setting.
Required: resourceId (path) — The ID of the resource (server, cron job, postgres, or redis) whose log streams should be returned

GET /v1/logs/streams/owner/{ownerId}
Returns log stream information for the specified workspace.
Required: ownerId (path) — The ID of the workspace to return log stream information for

GET /v1/logs/streams/resource/{resourceId}
Returns log stream override information for the specified resource. A log stream override takes precedence over a workspace's default log stream.
Required: resourceId (path) — The ID of the resource (server, cron job, postgres, or redis) to return log stream override information for

PUT /v1/logs/streams/owner/{ownerId}
Updates log stream information for the specified workspace. All logs for resources owned by this workspace will be sent to this log stream unless overridden by individual resources.
Required: ownerId (path) — The ID of the workspace to update log stream information for; body (body)

PUT /v1/logs/streams/resource/{resourceId}
Updates log stream override information for the specified resource. A log stream override takes precedence over a workspace's default log stream.
Required: resourceId (path) — The ID of the resource (server, cron job, postgres, or redis) to update log stream override information for; body (body)
